WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:51.230
Coming off of a pretty mediocre debate performance,
Joe Biden almost immediately went to a restaurant

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.460
and made a sort of bizarre comment about a
gay waiter.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:01.000
That is again just making me wonder about
Joe Biden's judgment in telling these stories

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.550
and anecdotes.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.129
This is two days after the debate.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:08.630
On Saturday, there was a fundraiser for Joe
Biden hosted by a public relations executive

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:09.630
in Seattle.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:16.259
And Biden was, I guess trying to talk about
how far we've come as a society on gay rights.

00:01:16.259 --> 00:01:22.060
And he said to the crowd five years ago, if
someone in Seattle made fun of a gay waiter

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.170
at a restaurant, people would have just quote,
let it go.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.700
And people in the crowd found it really odd.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:32.420
And they actually started yelling out, no,
we wouldn't have five years ago in Seattle.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:36.930
We wouldn't have let someone maybe making
fun of the gay waiter, just go.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:42.679
And the pool report from the event sums it
up as Biden saying basically if today someone

00:01:42.679 --> 00:01:47.450
made a homophobic comment in Seattle to a
gay waiter, that person would not be invited

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.450
back to the restaurant.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.509
They'd be asked to leave and would be told
not to come back.

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:53.209
But that five years ago you could get away
with that in Seattle.

00:01:53.209 --> 00:01:55.460
You could get away with making fun of a gay
waiter.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.179
So look at how far we've come.

00:01:57.179 --> 00:01:58.179
Now.

00:01:58.179 --> 00:01:59.179
It's a strange comment.

00:01:59.179 --> 00:02:04.149
I get the idea, which is we've just come so
far, but the problem is that it makes Joe

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:08.539
Biden seem out of touch with Seattle because
Seattle has been very much on the forefront

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:09.539
of gay rights.

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:11.039
It's been very forward thinking.

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:16.290
So it seems kind of out of touch to suggest
that in 2014 which is pretty late in the game

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:20.599
for the more progressive states that making
fun of a gay waiter would be acceptable in

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:21.599
any sense.

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:25.770
So I do want to say this is a bit of a pylon
with Joe Biden.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:29.680
There is a lot to criticize Joe Biden for
Joe Biden is not someone I'm interested in

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.510
voting for in the Democratic primary.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.540
Joe Biden's debate performance wasn't good.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.480
Joe Biden straight up said he's not for Medicare
for all.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.290
He wants to tweak Obamacare.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:41.300
There's a ton of stuff to criticize Joe Biden
about.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:47.129
He has a strange history of saying positive
things about segregation as elected officials,

00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:50.720
but overall he is actually saying the right
things about LGBT rights.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.099
He pointed out that even though gay marriage
is now legal in 50 states, you can still get

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:58.260
fired over your sexual orientation in 22 states.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.069
That's a huge issue.

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:02.050
It doesn't get nearly enough attention.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.659
Joe Biden is right to bring it up and I'm
glad that he's doing it.

00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:08.349
The comment about Seattle, it's dumb.

00:03:08.349 --> 00:03:11.819
It shows he doesn't really know very much
about Seattle.

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:13.530
Seattle was way ahead on this stuff.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:17.200
They passed the Fair Employment Practice Ordinance
in the early Seventies.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.390
They've had benefits for same sex partners
for a long time in Washington state for as

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.969
long as Joe Biden has been in politics.

00:03:24.969 --> 00:03:28.540
Maybe some of this stuff does feel relatively
recent.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:33.459
Like when you've been in politics, as long
as Joe Biden, something happening in 2014

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:36.870
or 2004 might feel almost like the same thing.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:42.109
I actually don't think we should be making
as big of a deal about this because Joe Biden

00:03:42.109 --> 00:03:47.659
basically is right on gay rights in almost
all cases at this point in time.

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:50.980
Uh, there are much bigger fish to fry when
it comes to Joe Biden.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:56.370
So if you believe that Joe Biden making this
comment is anything more than just being out

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:59.780
of touch with Seattle politics over the last
couple of decades.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:02.829
I'm open to having my mind changed.

00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:06.239
If people in the audience want to get in touch
and tell me how I'm misinterpreting it.

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:10.739
Out of touch, comment Joe Biden bringing up
important issues actually about gay rights

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:15.329
and there are far bigger criticisms that we
can and should be making about Joe Biden's

00:04:15.329 --> 00:04:17.170
policy in other areas, including on healthcare.

